## Merged feature sources (ideas reimplemented in TypeScript — no source code copied)

The iOS app also brings together the best ideas from four more open-source music players.
Every feature below was written from scratch for this codebase. They are credited in the
in-app About & Credits screen as well.

- **Spotube** by [KRTirtho](https://github.com/KRTirtho/spotube). License: AGPL-3.0.
  Ideas used: artist/song blacklist, scrobbling, first-run welcome, queue editing, per-song
  lyrics delay, skipping non-music segments (SponsorBlock), named file export. No Spotube code is
  included. Spotube's AGPL-3.0 license notice is kept here as a courtesy.
- **OpenSpot Music** by [BlackHatDevX](https://github.com/BlackHatDevX/openspot-music-app). License: MIT.
  Ideas used: Spotify public playlist import (here it reads the public embed page instead of a
  third-party transfer service), trending charts by country, capsule mini player, quick actions,
  offline banner.
- **Musike** by [Ernani1234](https://github.com/Ernani1234/musike). License: MIT.
  Ideas used: "Search a list" batch matching with swap, paste-a-YouTube-link, search
  suggestions, multi-select, backup export/import with merge/replace preview, accent presets plus a
  custom colour, hideable Home sections, autoplay radio, queue resume, next-track preload, and a
  remote YouTube client list (`config/streaming.json`).
- **Cog** by [Christopher Snowhill (kode54) and contributors](https://github.com/losnoco/Cog). License: GPL-2.0.
  Ideas used: ReplayGain-style normalisation with clipping prevention, spectrum visualizer,
  Last.fm and ListenBrainz scrobbling, playing files from the iOS Files app, hold next/previous to
  seek.

Copyright notices for the MIT-licensed projects:
- OpenSpot Music: Copyright (c) BlackHatDevX. MIT License.
- Musike: Copyright (c) Ernani1234. MIT License.

Charts data comes from Apple's public iTunes RSS feeds. Non-music segment data comes from
SponsorBlock (https://sponsor.ajay.app, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 database), and can be turned off in Settings. Scrobbles go to Last.fm and
ListenBrainz only when you connect your own account.

Extra catalogues and data: indie tracks stream from Audius (https://audius.co, artist uploads via
its open API). Live stations come from the community-run Radio Browser directory
(https://www.radio-browser.info). Artist bios are short excerpts from Wikipedia
(https://www.wikipedia.org), licensed CC BY-SA 4.0, and always link to the source article.

Ambient light reads artwork colours with jpeg-js (https://github.com/jpeg-js/jpeg-js, BSD-3-Clause,
Copyright (c) 2014 Eugene Ware, based on pdf.js by Mozilla, Apache-2.0).

The iOS widget extension is added to the Xcode project at prebuild time by @bacons/apple-targets
(https://github.com/EvanBacon/expo-apple-targets, MIT, Copyright (c) Evan Bacon). Song details and
covers for "Edit song info" are looked up through Apple's iTunes Search API and the Deezer API.

## Rename notice — HolySic

In November 2026 this fork was renamed to **HolySic**, with a new name, logo, bundle identifier
(`com.holysic.music`) and internal code names. HolySic is a modified version of Mochy Music:
realidkroo's original app lives at https://github.com/realidkroo/Mochy-Music and remains under
GPL-3.0. Every notice above is kept unchanged, and HolySic stays free with no ads or paywalls.
Library backups exported from the older build can still be imported.
